# What Vercel does NOT need in order to build the web app.
#
# Without this file Vercel uploads the whole repository — 420 MB, including a 180 MB Electron binary —
# and refuses the deploy outright, because no single file may exceed 100 MB:
#
#     Error: File size limit exceeded (100 MB)
#
# Every package.json stays, on purpose. Vercel runs pnpm with CI=1, which makes it use
# --frozen-lockfile, and a lockfile that lists a workspace the upload has removed is a different
# failure. So the packages remain and only their build output goes.

# ── stated outright rather than trusted to a default ──
# Vercel does ignore these on its own, but this deploy already failed once on a file-size limit and
# the local .next/cache alone holds a 105 MB and a 125 MB webpack pack. Vercel installs its own
# dependencies and runs its own build, so uploading either is useless as well as fatal.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.vercel
.git

# ── the desktop app's build output: 340 MB, and the reason the deploy was refused ──
# The web app serves this installer from disk at /api/download/windows when it is present, which is
# what lets a till download it over the LAN. On Vercel it is absent, the route answers 404, and the
# /get page falls back to NEXT_PUBLIC_DOWNLOAD_WINDOWS. Both paths are intended.
apps/desktop/dist

# ── other build output nothing here needs ──
apps/mobile/.expo
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/ios
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/.next-dev

# ── source material, not the product: 49 MB of artwork and the written guides ──
design
backups
*.pdf
*.docx

# …except the manual, which the app serves for download at /DineFlow-Manual.pdf
!apps/web/public/*.pdf

# ── local-only, and never any business of a deployment ──
box
*.bat
*.command
start.sh
